# Example env file for `docker compose --env-file apex.env up`.
# Copy to apex.env and fill in. On the DO apex droplet, Terraform writes this file
# for you from terraform.tfvars (deploy/digitalocean-apex/) — you only edit it by
# hand when running the compose stack on some other Docker host.

# Hostname Caddy gets a TLS cert for and serves the SPA on. Must resolve (A
# record) to this host before the cert can be issued.
APEX_DOMAIN=tenshu.app

# Contact email for the Let's Encrypt account (cert-expiry notices).
ACME_EMAIL=admin@tenshu.app

# Pin which prebuilt image to pull (a short git sha is safer than `latest` — you
# know exactly what's running and can roll back). Unset => latest.
# APEX_IMAGE_TAG=1a2b3c4

# The relay origin compiled INTO the SPA. ⚠ Only takes effect on the ON-BOX build
# path (`up -d --build`) — a prebuilt image already has the relay URL baked in at
# CI build time (pass it as the workflow's build-arg there instead). Defaults to
# the production relay; set it only if your relay lives on a different host.
# VITE_TENSHU_RELAY_URL=https://relay.tenshu.app

# Origin of the commerce service the account/purchase surface talks to. Compiled
# INTO the SPA (same on-box-build caveat as VITE_TENSHU_RELAY_URL above).
#
# ⚠⚠ The commerce service must itself be started with WEB_APP_ORIGIN set to THIS
# apex's origin, or every call from the browser dies in CORS preflight with no
# response to inspect. The service is native-only by default, deliberately.
# VITE_TENSHU_COMMERCE_URL=https://commerce.service.tenshu.app

# Pre-launch signup gate. Any non-empty value closes the door behind "Get started": the marketing
# site stays public, but realm creation, device pairing and try-mode are all unreachable and
# /onboarding renders a "not open yet" notice instead. Existing realms in a visitor's browser are
# untouched — they can still unlock and open the control plane.
#
# Unset/empty (the default) = signup open. That is deliberately the zero-config state, so a test
# deployment of the WORKING site needs nothing set here and only the public deploy carries the knob.
#
# ⚠ Same on-box-build caveat as the two URLs above: Vite inlines this at BUILD time, so flipping it
# means rebuilding the SPA, not just restarting the container.
# ⚠ A curtain, not security. The relay's endpoints are unchanged; this only stops the site pointing
# at them. Genuine gating belongs at the relay.
# VITE_SIGNUP_DISABLED=1
